Explain why logs may not appear immediately after enabling logging

Server access logs may not appear immediately because:
- Delivery is best-effort and is not guaranteed for every request.
- Log delivery is delayed and can take several hours.
- The destination bucket permissions may be incorrect.
- The logging destination or prefix may be configured incorrectly.
- There may not have been enough qualifying requests to generate log entries.

Example: After enabling logging, upload a test object or perform another request against the source bucket. Wait several hours and check the destination bucket for log files.
